          <briefdescription>
          </briefdescription>
          <detaileddescription>
<para>RESERVED AND CURRENTLY UNUSED. Would report a model whose variant declares a hard device requirement the host cannot meet. No catalog model declares one, so the check is deliberately not built — the number is reserved so the taxonomy has a documented home for it, and so nobody assigns 6007 to something else. Client placement requests are <emphasis>hints</emphasis> and cannot error: they are downgraded and the resolved value is reported instead. See engine-selection-and-model-placement-spec.md section 7.4. </para>
          </detaileddescription>
