          <initializer>= 6008</initializer>
          <briefdescription>
          </briefdescription>
          <detaileddescription>
<para>A referenced model needs an engine that is not registered in this server build. The message names the model, its role, and the engine it needs.</para>
<para>This is a statement about the <emphasis>server binary</emphasis>, not about client bookkeeping. Through the first cut of protocol v13 the same number meant &quot;your session
did not declare this engine&quot; (<computeroutput>EngineNotDeclared</computeroutput>), which put the blame on a client field that is now advisory — and named a cause the reader could not act on. The guard that belongs earlier is the build-time one (spec §7.10). </para>
          </detaileddescription>
        </enumvalue>
