        <enumvalue id="_tryll_error_code_8h_1a360da770ac4dbf26ed954170d352944da29ed058f63cd9cf78f5565741a0b08c2" prot="public">
          <name>InvalidHotwordsScore</name>
          <initializer>= 4107</initializer>
          <briefdescription>
          </briefdescription>
          <detaileddescription>
<para>CreateVoiceInputRequest.hotwords_score is not a finite, non-negative number. It reaches the recognizer&apos;s beam search as a per-token bonus, so a NaN poisons every hypothesis comparison and an infinity makes the biased path win unconditionally — both surface as garbled transcripts with nothing in the log, which is why this is refused rather than clamped. </para>
          </detaileddescription>
        </enumvalue>
